; einargudni.com — records to import into Cloudflare (DNS > Records > Import)
;
; Verified against ns2.vercel-dns.com on 2026-09-14 by classifying every name:
; a host is EXPLICIT if it has a CNAME, or an A that differs from the wildcard's
; answer (216.150.x.x). "Returns a Vercel 404" proves nothing — the wildcard
; answers every name, so a 404 is what a *missing* record looks like too.
;
; Not expressible in a zone file, do separately:
;   - apex + www + posture + nido  -> see the wildcard note below
;   - proxy status (orange/grey)   -> set by hand after import
;
; THE WILDCARD IS LOAD-BEARING. www, posture and nido have no records of their
; own; they resolve only through `*` and are routed by Host header at Vercel.
; Either keep the wildcard, or give each of those three an explicit record
; before dropping it. Dropping it blind takes down the main site and both apps.

$ORIGIN einargudni.com.
$TTL 300

; --- apps on Vercel, explicit A records (legacy anycast IP) ----------------
craft           300  IN  A      76.76.21.21
writing         300  IN  A      76.76.21.21

; --- apps elsewhere --------------------------------------------------------
learning        300  IN  A      66.241.124.56          ; Fly.io
learnings       300  IN  CNAME  remix-workbook.fly.dev.
coolify         300  IN  A      37.27.184.91           ; Hetzner, self-hosted

; --- already on Cloudflare Pages ------------------------------------------
sologbjor       300  IN  CNAME  sol-og-bjor.pages.dev.

; --- Resend email. Not on the apex, which is why an apex-only MX/TXT check
; --- wrongly reads as "this domain has no email". Losing these breaks DKIM
; --- and SPF for the contact form's own sending.
send            300  IN  MX     10 feedback-smtp.us-east-1.amazonses.com.
send            300  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all"
resend._domainkey 300 IN TXT    "p=MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQCtw/Uu5q6LnG6awwgvHQ7W5NqqptFbekke6/GGAjMae3ttqLMujzOfPLKWcsQcjzdrIIs6vScDn6Lutai/6E/gIRU543g8UuIy/Odn2UdHB/FCMY9ZWBITTA633qJ1qmth8a0QMi3zWuARk8iiWXK3zQyZFG+sK1aURraA60cPMwIDAQAB"

; --- certificate authority authorisation ----------------------------------
; letsencrypt.org and pki.goog are the two issuers Cloudflare Universal SSL
; uses, so these carry across unchanged and certs provision without edits.
@               300  IN  CAA  0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
@               300  IN  CAA  0 issue "pki.goog"
@               300  IN  CAA  0 issue "sectigo.com"
